<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>geocog</id>
    <version>__VERSION__</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/kartoza/geocog/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>kartoza</owners>
    <title>geocog</title>
    <authors>Kartoza (Pty) Ltd</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/kartoza/geocog</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kartoza/geocog/main/resources/geocog.png</iconUrl>
    <copyright>2026 Kartoza (Pty) Ltd</copyright>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/kartoza/geocog/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/kartoza/geocog</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://kartoza.github.io/geocog/</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/kartoza/geocog/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>cog gdal vrt minio s3 geoserver tui gis raster geospatial</tags>
    <summary>A small, fast TUI and toolkit for the GeoTIFF → COG → object storage → GeoServer VRT workflow.</summary>
    <description>
geocog turns ordinary GeoTIFFs into cloud-hosted Cloud Optimized GeoTIFFs
(COGs), uploads them to S3/MinIO, and wraps one or more of them in a single
GeoServer-ready GDAL VRT — all from a keyboard-driven terminal UI plus matching
CLI tools.

This package installs the geocog MSI. **GDAL** (and, for uploads, the MinIO
client `mc`) must be available on PATH for conversion/upload/VRT steps:

    choco install gdal
    </description>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="gdal" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
